          "worked": "The reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Sine is positive in the first and second quadrants.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(\\theta)&=\\frac12\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\text{ or }\\pi-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\text{ or }\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth angles lie in $[0,2\\pi)$, so the event is $\\left\\{\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\right\\}$.",
